<title>JAPAN: Japan oil operation not affected by Typhoon Violet.</title>
<headline>Japan oil operation not affected by Typhoon Violet.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>No damage to Japanese oil facilities have been reported so far after typhoon Violet hit the country's pacific coast on Sunday, the Petroleum Association of Japan (PAJ) said.</p>
<p>&quot;We've received no report of typhoon's damage to Japan's oil facilities and their operation,&quot; a PAJ official said on Monday.</p>
<p>At least seven people were killed and more than 40 were injured in central Japan on Sunday when Typhoon Violet, the 17th typhoon to hit the country this year, stormed along the Pacific coast. The typhoon caused blackouts to more than 70,000 homes, and flooded some 3,000 others.</p>
